{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1437730-where-is-the-crunch-for-dark-eras","id":1437730,"title":"Where is the \"crunch\" for Dark Eras?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-03-02T19:37:29-08:00","id":1437730,"title":"Where is the \"crunch\" for Dark Eras?","content":"<span style=\"color:#222222\"> I've been going through the Dark Eras books and they seem to be conspicuously missing a lot of what I'd expect to find, especially with regard to equipment. There don't seem to be any sailing rules or longship stats in the viking era, for instance. The Neolithic, Hellenistic, and Three Kingdoms chapters have a handful of new weapon and armor types, but I can't find something as simple as a Norse battle axe, and there don't seem to be rules for any kind of pre-modern firearms in <i>any</i> of the chapters, despite there being a Hunter tactic focused on them which is simply bizarre. Shield walls are mentioned, but there are no mechanics for them. There are NPCs who will have, say, a Greatsword as part of their stat block but no actual rules for giving a player a greatsword. Am I missing something? I have the searchable PDF and I feel like I've exhausted all of the keywords that would get these to come up.<br /> <br /> </span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4953-asatj","name":"AsaTJ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4953_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-02T22:13:59-08:00","id":1437756,"title":"","content":"Are you only looking at Dark Eras 1 or at multiple of the books?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-03T00:39:34-08:00","id":1437767,"title":"","content":"Hurt Locker has Battle Axes and Great Swords. Sailing got rules in the Pirate Dark Era, but as Vikings were raiders and their ships weren't actually part of battle they didn't get them.<br /> <br /> Flintlocks were put into the Dark Eras Companion.<br /> <br /> &quot;Flintlocks take five turns to reload. Stats are below:<br /> Pistol: Damage 2, Range 15/30/60, Clip 1, Initiative -2, Strength 2, Size 2<br /> Musket: Damage 3, Range 30/60/120, Clip 1, Initiative -5, Strength 3, Size 4&quot;<br /> <br /> For the most part there's not going to be a mechanical difference between a Norse battle ax and a battle ax, as there's a wide variety of slightly different weapons with different names but ending up doing, for storytelling purposes, the same thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-03T05:35:54-08:00","id":1437801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1437730-where-is-the-crunch-for-dark-eras?p=1437767#post1437767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but as Vikings were raiders and their ships weren't actually part of battle they didn't get them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except all the times that they were. It's not what longships were built for, but vikings were pragmatists and they absolutely pirated other ships when such opportunities arose. Longships were also used in combat between various norse rulers, especially when attempting to pass or protect strategic water passages. It's not the main use, but it definitely happened with some regularity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}